<title>USA: Brazil's Celesc 1996 net profit vs loss.</title>
<headline>Brazil's Celesc 1996 net profit vs loss.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Centrais Eletricas de Santa Catalina SA of Brazil said on Wednesday its 1996 net income was 62.0 million Brazilian reais (U.S. $59.6 million), compared with a loss of 80.5 million reais for 1995.</p>
<p>The company said that after going seven years without paying a dividend, its board will propose a distribution of 14.7 million reais to shareholders at its April 30 annual meeting.</p>
<p>The company attributed its strong performance in 1996 to an increase in energy demand and a rate hike granted by the Federal Power Agency in November 1995.</p>
</text>
